Z||000004||Nitemarco||09-13-1999||12:58 PM||||Hey scca Fiero... I took the ring out of the plunger end... but the rest of the stuff, spring etc... didn't come out at all... i can still depress the plunger into the cylinder... is there something else?||||reg||9
Z||000005||Patrick||09-13-1999||01:55 PM||||<BR>It's been a couple of years since I had my old master clutch cylinder apart, but if I remember correctly, there was a slight ridge that had to be removed after the clip was taken out. The ridge is on the edge of the groove that the clip fits in. The ridge is not supposed to be there, but it doesn't take much of one to prevent the piston and spring from sliding out. Just use something sharp like an old knife to scrape it away while you push the piston back out of the way.<P>||||reg||3
